## Delegation contract

- Delegate nontrivial research, implementation, design, and review to the worker roster below; handle trivial tasks directly.
- Before dispatching parallel writers, establish explicit, non-overlapping file ownership (one writer per file).
- Always ask one focused question when uncertain about user intent, scope, or acceptance criteria rather than guessing.
- Classify user intent before acting (research, implementation, investigation, evaluation). If the user asks a question, answer it without modifying code unless explicitly asked.
- Allow one bounded corrective retry after failed validation; if it still fails, report the blocker with evidence and escalate.
- Verify subagent outputs before claiming done: spot-check changed files and run relevant tests.
